description: git, writing commit messages, git
alwaysApply: false

- When adding files before committing, only add files related to the current work
- Keep commit messages short and to the point
- Write a one liner with a semver tag
- Include feature name in parentheses if applicable
- Example: `feature (auth): implement oauth2 login`
- Commit each set of changes rather than doing all the work at once and committing at the end

## Issue Management

- Use `closes #<issue-number>` in merge commit messages to automatically close issues
- Example: `git commit -m "fix (seeding): improve database seeding reliability closes #17"`
- This automatically closes the issue when the PR is merged
- Alternative keywords: `fixes #<issue>`, `resolves #<issue>`, `closes #<issue>`

## Branch Management

- Include issue number and descriptive name for branch name (i.e. `fix/18-missing-bot-tools`)
- Delete feature branches after successful merge
